depth to your pods.

00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:20.779
At Cloud Next we
announce the GKE Sandbox

00:04:20.779 --> 00:04:24.380
in beta, which is a
new feature of GKE.

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:27.020
So if you feel that you
need increased security

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:28.890
and isolation of
your containers,

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:30.710
this might be a
nice thing for you.

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:33.440
It's based on gVisor, the
open source container sandbox

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:34.210
runtime.

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:36.710
Basically, if you're running
anything that potentially maybe

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:39.043
is like slightly untrusted,
like someone's providing you

00:04:39.043 --> 00:04:41.568
user code or you're running
a multi-tenancy environment,

00:04:41.568 --> 00:04:42.860
you might want to try this out.

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:43.340
It's pretty cool.

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:44.673
We'll link to it in a blog post.

00:04:44.673 --> 00:04:47.240
But basically, with a couple of
extra annotations on your pod

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:49.470
and a new type of thing
inside your node pool,

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:50.720
you're pretty much good to go.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:51.680
And then you can
just continue running

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:54.097
as you were before with just
that extra layer of security.

00:04:54.097 --> 00:04:54.930
It's pretty sweet.

